Section: video
Priority: optional
Description: Hardware video decoding for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai, SM8750)
 Userspace stack for the Qualcomm Iris hardware video decoder (the Venus
 lineage, "Iris Decoder" V4L2 node, qcom_iris kernel module) of the OnePlus
 Pad 3. Ships the iris-vaapi VA-API driver (iris_drv_video.so) so VA-API
 clients drive /dev/videoN directly, plus all browser integration:
 . - /etc/environment.d/55: LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=iris (libva cannot autodetect
   the driver on msm platform devices)
 . - /etc/environment.d/56: MOZ_DISABLE_RDD_SANDBOX=1 (Firefox VA-API decode
   runs in the RDD process, whose seccomp sandbox blocks /dev/dma_heap)
 . - /etc/firefox/policies/policies.json: locked VA-API decode prefs
 . - /etc/chromium.d/erhai-hw-video: AcceleratedVideoDecoder feature flag
   (chromium's V4L2VideoDecoder drives the iris node directly, no VA-API)
 . - /etc/brave/policies/managed/erhai-hwvideo.json: HardwareAccelerationMode
 . - udev rule giving the video group access to /dev/dma_heap/system
 Codecs: H.264, HEVC Main/Main10, VP9 Profile 0/2 (no AV1). Chromium
 (xtradeb) decodes H.264/VP9 via V4L2; Firefox and Brave decode H.264/HEVC
 Main (and Main10/VP9 P2 where the firmware exposes P010) via VA-API.
 Requires oneplus-erhai-linux-7.2 >= +b10 (decode-order output property) for
 Firefox/Brave; works out of the box in the full erhai image. After
 installing on a running desktop, log out and back in once.
 .
 The iris-vaapi source tree ships in /usr/src/oneplus-erhai-video/iris-vaapi.

